    "type": "text",
    "text": "## What happened\n\n1. **Password brute force.** `198.51.100.42` sent ~18k `POST /login` requests (almost all `401`) from `python-requests`. That's ~85% of all traffic overnight.\n2. **Report timeouts.** `/api/report` returned 94 `504`s: the backend can't finish within `proxy_read_timeout` while the workers are busy with logins.\n3. The rest is normal traffic: the product catalog and static files with `304`.\n\n## What to fix\n\nRate-limit the login and give the heavy report its own location:\n\n```nginx\nlimit_req_zone $binary_remote_addr zone=login:10m rate=5r/m;\n\nserver {\n    location = /login {\n        limit_req zone=login burst=10 nodelay;\n        limit_req_status 429;\n        proxy_pass http://app;\n    }\n\n    location = /api/report {\n        proxy_read_timeout 120s;\n        proxy_pass http://app;\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThen apply it: `nginx -t && systemctl reload nginx`. If the attacks keep coming, add a fail2ban jail on `401` for `/login`.",
